{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1350,
 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why are 500 men lifting a hotel with the guests still inside?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.57
  },
  {
   "text": "Upstairs, a man pours his tea. If one jack slips, six floors fall.",
   "s": 3.87,
   "e": 7.51
  },
  {
   "text": "The whole city laughed at them. Lift a hotel? With screws?",
   "s": 7.71,
   "e": 10.345
  },
  {
   "text": "So the boss blows a whistle, and every man gives his jack one turn.",
   "s": 10.645,
   "e": 14.125
  },
  {
   "text": "The hotel rises the width of a hair. Then another hair. Then another.",
   "s": 14.325,
   "e": 17.575
  },
  {
   "text": "But then the walls groan, and a crack shoots up the bricks!",
   "s": 17.775,
   "e": 20.056
  },
  {
   "text": "People sprint out of the street. The man upstairs? Still pouring tea.",
   "s": 20.256,
   "e": 23.455
  },
  {
   "text": "So why would anyone lift a hotel at all?",
   "s": 23.655,
   "e": 25.458
  },
  {
   "text": "Because Chicago was sinking. The mud was so deep, wagons vanished in it.",
   "s": 25.758,
   "e": 29.266
  },
  {
   "text": "One sign in the street said, in big letters: No bottom here.",
   "s": 29.466,
   "e": 32.484
  },
  {
   "text": "So the city decided to raise everything, and build sewers underneath.",
   "s": 32.684,
   "e": 35.91
  },
  {
   "text": "The whistle blows one last time.",
   "s": 36.31,
   "e": 37.731
  },
  {
   "text": "The hotel stands six feet taller, and the tea never spilled.",
   "s": 37.931,
   "e": 41.1
  },
  {
   "text": "And the guests? Nobody even bothered to tell them.",
   "s": 41.3,
   "e": 43.497
  }
 ],
